@@ -63,6 +63,21 @@ fwctl --device sensor-0042 update sensor-node-1.2.0.fwpkg
 fwctl --device sensor-0042 status
 ```
 
+Field work often has to split the transfer from the reboot. `stage` pushes and
+verifies the image while the device keeps running its confirmed firmware, and
+`activate` finishes the update later from the staging journal alone:
+
+```sh
+fwctl --device sensor-0042 stage sensor-node-1.2.0.fwpkg
+fwctl staged
+fwctl --device sensor-0042 activate
+```
+
+A staged record is kept per device, and re-staging replaces it. Activation
+consumes the record whatever the outcome; if the device no longer matches what
+was staged, activation stops before boot state moves and the image must be
+staged again.
+
 After an update, run `fwctl --device sensor-0042 history` to review the outcome
 recorded locally, or `fwctl doctor` if a device does not show up in `fwctl
 devices`.
